{"id": "EUVD-2026-107885", "enisaUuid": "0562a6a9-a900-3682-9b21-2bb55ea68447", "description": "Roundcube Webmail before 1.6.20 and 1.7.x before 1.7.5 is affected by an IMAP command injection vulnerability. A remote authenticated attacker can exploit this via CRLF sequences injected into the _flag parameter of the mail/mark action to execute arbitrary IMAP commands. Upstream fixed this in the commit \u201cFix IMAP command injection via CRLF in `_flag` parameter of mail/mark action\u201d, which rejects flags containing control, whitespace and IMAP-special characters.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T01:32:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T01:32:44", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://bugs.debian.org/1151279", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/commit/6c3c1897c11e193e47fccaabc87e9ca2a0a73e51", "https://roundcube.net/news/2026/10/19/security-updates-1.6.20-and-1.7.5", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/releases/tag/1.7.5", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/releases/tag/1.6.20", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/commit/242c6d6a150c850bd96d20d400261e71f8d11f9b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114720", "GHSA-3p38-q93v-93w8"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.81, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "57cd03a8-f433-3f0c-aecb-1ac062d6b938", "product": {"name": "Webmail", "vendor": {"name": "bulwarkmail"}}, "product_version": "1.7.0 <1.7.5"}, {"id": "6ee889da-9a0b-393e-b9b1-8c7ae9f321fd", "product": {"name": "Webmail", "vendor": {"name": "bulwarkmail"}}, "product_version": "1.6.0 <1.6.20"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "28169777-5e1d-3980-bfcd-d00b7e27804d", "vendor": {"name": "Roundcube"}}], "isExploited": false}